Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:09:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] fix(tools): a terminal call cut at the foreground limit
 says so

RHOAI3 v32: an M1 capture call requested timeout=7170 (a Kanban worker's
TERMINAL_MAX_FOREGROUND_TIMEOUT, derived from the task's max runtime, lets
the terminal tool accept it) and was cut by the executor's per-call deadline
(tools.sequential_call / tools.concurrent_batch, 420s by default). The tool
result said only "timed out after 420.0s", so the worker retried the same
foreground call.

The deadline is where the requested timeout is clamped: it is applied
whatever the call asked for, and the cut interrupts the worker thread, which
makes the terminal tool's foreground wait kill the process. For a foreground
terminal call the timeout result (sequential and concurrent paths) now keeps
the existing first sentence and adds: the process was killed at the
foreground limit, the requested and applied limits, and that a longer
command needs terminal(background=true, notify_on_complete=true) and then
process(action="wait") with a timeout below the limit, repeated until the
process exits. Other tools and background calls keep the plain message. The
limit's value is unchanged. Local extension.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
